import examples/bim-slice/bim_editor_core.dl

function check boundary move {boolean:condition} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function point boundary move at {cad vector2:spot} in {a pointer to a bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        move bim editor pointer to spot within 0.05 in editor
        if bim editor sketches upright (@intrinsic("dereference", editor)):
            move bim editor sketch pointer to spot within 0.05 in editor

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set modelTarget to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set corners to an empty list of a cad vector2
append (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to corners
append (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 0.0) to corners
append (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 4.0) to corners
append (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 4.0) to corners
set layers to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "test", 0.2)) to layers
set wallType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Wall") with layers to modelTarget
set wallId to add bim wall typed wallType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 0.0) to modelTarget
set floorId to add bim slab on editor's levelId around corners thick 0.2 to modelTarget
set roofType to add bim planar type named (the string form of "Roof") as role bim roof planar role with layers to modelTarget
set roofId to add bim slab on editor's levelId around corners thick 0.2 to modelTarget
set roofIndex to the bim slab index of roofId in editor's documentValue's current
set roofValue to the item at roofIndex's position in (editor's documentValue's current's slabs's values)
set roofValue's typeId to roofType
set roofValue's top to 2.0
set roofValue's pitch to @intrinsic("atan2", 0.5, 1.0)
replace item at index roofIndex's position in (editor's documentValue's current's slabs's values) with roofValue
loop hostCursor from 0 to 3:
    set hostId to floorId
    set hostKind to bim slab picked
    if hostCursor = 1:
        set hostId to roofId
    if hostCursor = 2:
        set hostId to wallId
        set hostKind to bim wall picked
    select bim editor hostKind numbered hostId in e
    open bim editor boundary sketch in e
    check boundary move (editor's sketchTool = bim sketch pick tool) named (the string form of "Tab starts in selection mode")
    set originalFile to the bim file text of editor's documentValue's current
    set firstPiece to the item at 0 in (editor's sketchSegments's values)
    point boundary move at firstPiece's start in e
    press bim editor boundary sketch in e
    check boundary move (bim boundary point selected in editor) named (the string form of "host endpoint selectable")
    type bim editor boundary key 71 in e
    set movedPoint to a cad vector2 with x (firstPiece's start's x - 1.0) and y firstPiece's start's y
    point boundary move at movedPoint in e
    set previewPiece to the bim displayed boundary segment at 0 of editor
    check boundary move (bim boundary point previewPiece's start meets movedPoint) named (the string form of "G previews the endpoint")
    check boundary move ((the bim file text of editor's documentValue's current) = originalFile) named (the string form of "preview leaves model unchanged")
    type bim editor boundary key bim escape key code in e
    check boundary move (bim boundary point (the bim selected boundary point of editor) meets firstPiece's start) named (the string form of "Escape cancels only the move")
    # Select the edge midpoint and translate it; both neighbours remain joined.
    set midpoint to a cad vector2 with x ((firstPiece's start's x + firstPiece's finish's x) * 0.5) and y ((firstPiece's start's y + firstPiece's finish's y) * 0.5)
    point boundary move at midpoint in e
    press bim editor boundary sketch in e
    check boundary move ((editor's sketchPicked = 0) and ((the length of (editor's editPicked's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "edge selected independently of points")
    type bim editor boundary key 71 in e
    point boundary move at (a cad vector2 with x midpoint's x and y (midpoint's y - 0.5)) in e
    press bim editor boundary sketch in e
    set movedEdge to the item at 0 in (editor's sketchSegments's values)
    check boundary move ((the absolute value of (movedEdge's start's y - (firstPiece's start's y - 0.5))) < 1e-8) named (the string form of "click places edge translation")
    set joined to the bim boundary loop of (editor's sketchSegments's values)
    check boundary move joined's valid named (the string form of "incident edges remain a valid loop")
    type bim editor boundary key 258 in e
    check boundary move (editor's editMode = false) named (the string form of "Tab commits the host contour")
    ignore undo bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
    check boundary move ((the bim file text of editor's documentValue's current) = originalFile) named (the string form of "one undo restores the host")

select bim editor bim slab picked numbered roofId in e
open bim editor boundary sketch in e
set roofSpot to the bim sketch world point of (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 2.0) for editor
set levelLift to the bim elevation of level editor's levelId in editor's documentValue's current
check boundary move ((the absolute value of (roofSpot's z - (levelLift + 4.0))) < 1e-8) named (the string form of "roof sketch follows actual pitch and top")
set ray to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ray record, (a cad vector3 with x 4.0, y 2.0 and z (levelLift + 10.0)), (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -1.0))
set roofHit to the bim sketch hit along ray for editor
check boundary move (roofHit's found and (bim boundary point roofHit's spot meets (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 2.0))) named (the string form of "roof picking uses displayed sketch plane")

# A model/plan snap must never leak into the host's own plane.
set editor's snap to the bim snap (a cad vector2 with x 999.0 and y 999.0) labelled "Wrong plane"
set snapValue to the bim sketch snap at (a cad vector2 with x 3.02 and y 0.01) of editor
check boundary move (snapValue's label = (the string form of "Mid point")) named (the string form of "local midpoint snap has priority")
set editor's snapOff to true
set snapValue to the bim sketch snap at (a cad vector2 with x 3.023 and y 0.017) of editor
check boundary move ((snapValue's point's x = 3.023) and (snapValue's point's y = 0.017)) named (the string form of "disabled snapping preserves the plane coordinates")
set editor's snapOff to false
set editor's sketchTool to bim sketch line tool
append (a cad vector2 with x 1.0 and y 1.0) to (editor's sketchPending's values)
set snapValue to the bim sketch snap at (a cad vector2 with x 2.0 and y 1.02) of editor
check boundary move ((snapValue's label = (the string form of "Horizontal")) and (snapValue's point's y = 1.0)) named (the string form of "tracking uses local plane axes")
check boundary move ((the bim ifc class of editor selection editor) = (the string form of "IfcSlab / ROOF")) named (the string form of "visible roof classification matches IFC export")

set basis to the bim object frame of editor
check boundary move ((basis's found and (basis's origin's x = 0.0)) and ((the absolute value of (basis's origin's z - (levelLift + 2.0))) < 1e-8)) named (the string form of "roof gizmo uses object origin")
check boundary move ((basis's xAxis's z > 0.4) and ((the absolute value of (the cad dot of basis's xAxis and basis's zAxis)) < 1e-8)) named (the string form of "roof local axes follow slope and remain perpendicular")
leave bim editor boundary sketch in e
begin bim editor gizmo drag in e
drag bim editor gizmo by (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) lifting 1.0 turning 0.0 about (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) in e
set basis to the bim object frame of editor
check boundary move ((the absolute value of (basis's origin's z - (levelLift + 3.0))) < 1e-8) named (the string form of "gizmo raises a roof top")
drag bim editor gizmo by (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) lifting 0.0 turning 0.0 about (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) in e
set basis to the bim object frame of editor
check boundary move ((the absolute value of (basis's origin's z - (levelLift + 2.0))) < 1e-8) named (the string form of "returning gizmo to zero restores original height")
finish bim editor gizmo drag in e
